course: dictionary
lesson: 11970
title: Caterer: the people who bring the food
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A caterer is a person or company whose job is to provide food and drinks for events such as parties, weddings and meetings. The verb is cater: to cater for a party means to supply the food for it.
explain: «The caterer made sandwiches for thirty guests at the wedding.» The clues are wedding, sandwiches and thirty guests. Someone had to make all that food, so the caterer is the person who did it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The ___ charged us five pounds for each guest.» Does caterer fit? Yes, so your meaning works. A caterer can be one person with a van or a big company with a team of cooks.
fact: A caterer provides food and drinks for events.
fact: «Caterer» is a noun, and «caterers» is the plural, meaning more than one caterer.
fact: The verb «cater» means to supply food for an event, as in «They cater for weddings.»
fact: People often hire a caterer for a wedding, a party or a big meeting.
fact: A caterer may charge per guest, so feeding 10 guests costs less than feeding 30.
exercise: «The caterer made sandwiches for thirty guests.» What is a caterer? | A place where people sit to eat | A type of birthday cake | A guest who arrives late to a party | *A person or company that provides food and drinks for events
exercise: Which word is the verb meaning to supply food for an event? | guests | caterer | *cater | wedding
exercise: Mum says, «We need to hire a caterer for the wedding.» Why would she do that? | To take photos of the wedding | To drive the guests home | *To get the food and drinks for the wedding | To sing at the wedding
test: «The caterer charges five pounds for each guest.» How much does the caterer charge for ten guests? | £5 | *£50 | £500 | £15
test: A wedding caterer is | a person who takes wedding photos | a church bell ringer | a dressmaker for the bride | *someone who supplies food and drinks for weddings
exam: Jayden says a caterer only cooks meals at home for his family. Is he right? | No, a caterer provides food for events such as parties and weddings | Yes, a caterer only cooks for families at home | Yes, a caterer only makes drinks | *No, a caterer is only a type of cake
